&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2025 4AD"]}, {"t": 19555, "time": "05:25:55", "artist": "Sault", "title": "S.O.T.H.", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Sault+S.O.T.H.", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Sault+S.O.T.H.", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Sault+S.O.T.H.", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Sault+S.O.T.H.", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1808467830", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Sault+S.O.T.H.", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Sault+S.O.T.H.&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2025 Forever Living Originals"]}, {"t": 19919, "time": "05:31:59", "artist": "Dianna Lopez", "title": "Meadow Spirit", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1816885419", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2025 888"]}, {"t": 20066, "time": "05:34:26", "artist": "Bartelbi", "title": "Light Pulse", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Bartelbi+Light+Pulse", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bartelbi+Light+Pulse", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Bartelbi+Light+Pulse", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Bartelbi+Light+Pulse", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1830938002", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Bartelbi+Light+Pulse", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Bartelbi+Light+Pulse&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2025 Bartelbi"]}], "counts": {"high": 1, "mid": 20, "low": 11}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:32:22", "end": "00:33:24", "text": "The Allnighter on FBi Radio 94.5 Sydney with us. Thank you."}, {"start": "00:33:31", "end": "00:34:17", "text": "The first three letters in Ngu means inner. Ra means emotional. That's the definition of home for Wal-Pi people and Central Australian people. Ngura, something that runs like a power source that keeps your body going. And that's your old ngura-kul history. Your language history, your sermon history, your skin name ceremony, and your law within that tribe. Yeah, your jurisdiction."}, {"start": "00:34:47", "end": "00:36:59", "text": "To exist in the homeland of the kangaroo, you have to understand. To understand it, we'll try and teach you to soar really high like the word snail. It's like reading a book. The behavior of animals, the behavior of change of character. Once you master that really well, flow from this country. It shapes us who we are. They call this crown land, I sometimes wonder what, what crown, ask you to find out the original crown of this country. In doing that, you are like a milvery, fulfilling your duty of care. We call it coterie. Crown is all because you fulfill something. Your fulfillment of carrying your country, giving back to you. And that's all the knowledge for your own well-being from this country, to give it back to people. In doing so, you already got the original crown. The emus crown. I am I am I am I am"}, {"start": "00:37:12", "end": "00:38:51", "text": "Yeah, the original crown is a southern cross here, because it's sitting on the emu's head. Yeah, to us, that's a whole murakulu. It's a reminder that we mustn't be like a little star drifting away. That's why the little stars is the homeland. or this continent and to learn all that one will expand your learning how you should live in this country and look firstly you must learn all these archives in the law the skin name the land the ceremony and the language To live in the home of the kangaroo, you have to understand the emu."}, {"start": "00:39:03", "end": "00:39:55", "text": "Your country will know you. I love you, I love you, I love you, I love you."}, {"start": "04:25:19", "end": "04:25:39", "text": "Mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm"}, {"start": "04:44:07", "end": "04:44:46", "text": "Five o'clock in the morning is, yeah, maybe four sometimes. Yeah, you see sunlight doesn't expand like we've always been drawing the sun coming up the mountains. Now, it shoots up, straight up to us, that's Kanoor. during this year in ceremony when the men sings women dance flicking their finger like that so they get to expand the light going this way horizontally"}, {"start": "04:45:15", "end": "04:46:02", "text": "First, you have to grow like a tree, straight up. That means, yeah, everything is born unto you. Everything around you, yeah, gonna be you. Embrace them while you can. Learn about them. Because they'll guide you how you should live. Because you're gonna have to adapt to this harsh country. and enjoy its richness, I guess, with that knowledge. Because if you don't, yeah, your birch ride is stripped from you and your life falls short. It's a really hard country out here."}, {"start": "04:47:43", "end": "04:48:28", "text": "The Allnighter on FBi Radio 94.5 Sydney with Andreas Mendoza. for creative, that's all."}], "fbi_json": [{"tim